    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301-a1">

                <pb facs="0472" n="376" xml:id="pg376"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 832.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Navy to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    your information a copy of a letter received from Rear-Admiral Dewey informing
                    this Department of the invaluable assistance Mr. E. H. Rawson-Walker, Her
                    Britannic Majesty’s consul at Manila, has been to him.</p>
                <p>This Department requests that your Department express to the British Government
                    the thanks of this Government for the services rendered to Admiral Dewey.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. H. Allen</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
